WEBVTT

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.980
I would like to see Dr. Shan.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.410
I'm sorry.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.470
Don't worry. It's always broken.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.120
Say, may I see Dr. Shan?

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.550
The Fusui doctor is inside,

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:09.520
but it's all up to his mood as to
whether you can see him or not.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.390
Here?

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:14.490
Go ahead and try. Since
you're so beautiful,

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.760
I'm pretty sure he'll see you.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:20.700
Thanks.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:30.010
Dr. Shan, are you in here?

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.570
Dr. Shan?

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.370
It's been a long time, Miss Stingray.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:04.470
Well, may I call you Little
Lady Sylia as I used to?

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.550
I'm glad you recognized me.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:08.520
Same to you.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.650
I'm impressed you didn't forget
this old man and came to visit me.

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.360
Honestly speaking, I have
a favor to ask, Doctor.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.790
Sure you do.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:20.760
The only reason I can think of that
you'd come here is to ask a favor.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.600
I'll help you in any way I can.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.300
I'm happy to hear you say that.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:31.070
Well, someone is trying to
release the seal of evil.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.100
Brian J. Mason.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.340
You already knew?

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.310
You know that Genom has been
digging earthworm holes

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.380
under Mega-Tokyo, don't you?

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.920
The stream of ground energy has
been constantly disrupted.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:52.090
They call the stream "Dragon
Line", which makes me laugh.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:56.500
Mason is seeking the Wiz Lab by
hiding behind that project.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:00.500
Yes, he's looking for the lab that
was buried under the earth.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.270
He keeps boring and missing
the target again and again.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:05.940
Missing the target?
Do you know...

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.040
Oh, no, I don't know where it is.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:15.570
It has been completely hidden by
the complex ground stream flow.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.850
However, regarding the
underground world,

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:21.760
I'm sure we know better
than Genom.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.260
I see.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.560
You came here to find out
where it is, didn't you?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:27.690
Yes.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:31.430
What are you going to do if you
find out where the place is?

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:36.800
Before Mason does anything
to it, I will seal it again.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:38.740
This time, perfectly!

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:44.610
I wonder if Dr. Stingray would
be happy about that.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:45.650
Doctor!

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:50.250
Oh, just a slip of the tongue,
an old man's nonsense.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:54.050
Forget about it. Well, have a seat.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.330
It's like I can't get a feel for this bike

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.330
when it's grabbing the surface of the road.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.590
The tires will be okay for a while.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.970
I used three parts around the suspension

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.360
and exchanged the chamber,
so it will be expensive.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.570
It happens.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.240
Oh, Nene, welcome.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.680
Hi ya!

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.340
Oh, it's unusual to see you here.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.620
Well, maybe not.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.240
I just came by, because I had nothing else to do.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.080
Oh yeah, Nene.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.390
Can you teach me how to remove
that protection you mentioned?

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:31.980
Uh, well...

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:36.290
Oh, Priss, what good timing.
Can I talk to you a second?

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.130
Sorry, Mackey. Next time!

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:47.200
Well, Miss, can you tell why I said
Mason's plan missed the target?

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:52.450
I guess Mason is seeking it based
on some old ungerground data,

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.850
but if a variable used
for prediction

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.690
of ground diastrophism is
off by even one percent,

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.120
there is a possibility of getting
exactly the opposite results.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.710
Sure, but it's the same...

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.890
Yes, it's the same for us too.

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:10.850
This shows the part of the stream
investigated by Genom.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.530
The data Mason has are dots,

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:17.670
but our data are lines.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:18.910
Then...

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.040
If we can figure out the variable,

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:25.740
I think we can pick only a few
points where the lab might be.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.880
Are you giving this data to me?

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.870
As a favor to my favorite little girl, and also...

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:35.610
We have invested much in that study.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.550
This is my atonement.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.060
Doctor...

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.030
Here!

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:47.770
Thank you.
Here!

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:48.500
Thank you.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:51.770
What do you want to talk about?

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:55.180
Well, how much do you
know about Sylia?

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.380
What kind of question is
that all the sudden?

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.810
Well, it's not a big deal.
I'm just curious about her.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:05.580
Let's see, you met her about
the same time I did.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.790
After I argued with the police
who closed that road,

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.550
she had a talk with me.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:13.330
Have you heard about
her younger days,

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:16.100
for example, about her
childhood or anything?

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.130
No, but I don't care about that.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:23.840
Well, Priss, I'm wondering why
Sylia created the Knight Sabers.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:24.940
Why ask now?

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.630
I wonder if this is all about her father?

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:32.770
You've heard of him, right? Dr. Stingray, the
person who developed boomers.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.640
Sylia has an instinctive hatred of
boomers, doesn't she?

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:42.220
Is that because Dr. Stingray is
the one who created them?

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:47.090
I don't know, but why are you
asking about things like that now?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.790
Well, Priss, actually, I...

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:54.900
Well, never mind. I'm not sure about it yet.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.470
About Mason...

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.010
That has nothing to do with a kid like you.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:06.480
But...

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.050
Sylia...

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:13.510
Nigel, I have something I need your help with.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:19.250
I'll be right in. Mackey, please finish up here.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.340
Dr. Stingray...

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:32.600
Died in the Tokyo Earthquake seven years ago.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:40.870
How about this? There! I got it!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.580
The word "impossible" doesn't exist for me.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:45.050
Let's see...

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:50.520
This can't be!

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.440
Here it is! As I thought,

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.100
the old data before the boomer
project was transferred to Wiz Lab.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:11.780
The mutant which was born in
the Core creation experiment...

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.300
I brought that thing you asked for.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.220
Ah, thank you, Nigel.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:17.550
Did you finish preparing the experiment?

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:19.620
All set.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.780
Put the sonar on the table.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:30.800
Done.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:34.400
Please check the readout of the sonar there.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.990
Well, let's start.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:42.140
If my hunch is right, that monster
is finding the boomers to eat

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:46.480
by seeking the peculiar vibration of boomers,

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.880
which transmits well underground.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.750
If so, how about this?

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:11.760
It looks good, doesn't it?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:17.010
Thank you, Nigel. I will be able to
ascertain the location of Wiz Lab.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:21.140
However, this machine's effective
range is only about 300 meters.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:24.920
It will take years to finish
covering all of Mega-Tokyo.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.390
Look here.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:35.920
I've narrowed it down to
twenty-seven candidate locations.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:40.100
I'm sure it won't be that difficult
to locate the correct one.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:44.090
I see. But if you find it, how are
you going to seal it again?

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.470
I will let Genom help me do that.

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:52.540
Genom? I don't think we can do
now what we couldn't do then.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:57.550
I came up with the idea while
checking data Dr. Shan gave me.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:00.280
There are things available now
which didn't exist seven years ago.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:04.180
This time, I'm going to get to
the root of the problem.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:44.560
Oh! It's already time!

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.050
I have to get back to the office.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:50.430
Well, I'm going to the studio.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.570
I didn't even guess that something
was wrong with Nene.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.770
I guess it's okay to leave her alone anyway.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:08.780
Have you asked Sylia?

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:13.460
I agree, it would seem like we're
investigating her private affairs,

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.830
but honestly speaking, I have
been a little curious.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:20.330
Why did Sylia start the Knight Sabers?

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:24.300
I know she has a lot of money
because of her father's patent,

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:26.170
but she gets nothing in return for doing this.

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:30.270
I'm sure that she doesn't simply
want to be a champion of right.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.670
You aren't satisfied by this answer?

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:35.970
Well, that sounds right.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.490
Oh, one more thing.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:49.330
No matter what private reasons
Sylia has, I think it's okay,

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:54.060
because I think we're all Knight
Sabers for our own reasons.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:13.120
Bring me the parts over there.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.590
Sure!

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:18.860
Excuse me...

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:19.460
Wrench.
Excuse me...

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:20.360
Wrench.
Yes, Sir!

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:20.920
Yes, Sir!

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.290
What did Sylia want?

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:29.000
Why don't you ask her?

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.130
She didn't tell me.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:34.840
Then, I can't tell you, can I?

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:36.180
I guess not.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:38.640
But I wonder if she intends to do
something dangerous, you know?

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:43.050
I don't know. I just made the thing
according to her specifications.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:45.020
I don't care what or how she uses it.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:48.010
Then, what was that order from Mason?

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:51.760
Muffler.

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:53.050
Didn't you hear me?

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:58.100
Let's take a break.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:02.300
Hello!

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.240
Ah, Nene...

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:04.870
Hi ya!
Ah, Nene...

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:05.700
Hi ya!

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:09.340
You'll have a cup of coffee, won't you?

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:11.140
Or is cocoa preferable for you?

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:19.920
Mackey, how old are you?

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:20.950
Fifteen.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.260
Your father was the famous
Dr. Stingray, wasn't he?

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:26.160
Say, what kind of father was he?

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.560
I don't remember much about him.

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:32.400
I was little, and he was
busy with his studies.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.090
Of course.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:37.800
Here's your cocoa.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:38.340
Thanks.
Here's your cocoa.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.270
Thanks.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:44.410
Well, till what age did you live with Sylia then?

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:47.780
Let's see, until eight years old. Why?

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:52.740
What? Well, I just wondered
what kind of kid Sylia was.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:56.980
I can't imagine what she was like.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:00.360
I guess she was an ordinary kid.

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:04.130
But she was smart even when she was little.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:08.230
Other people thought she was
cold, but she was gentle to me.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:11.540
I see. It sounds like she was
the same then as now.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:14.300
Oh, I meant she's gentle!

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.770
Well, what kind of kid were you, Mackey?

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:23.350
Me?

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:26.240
I haven't changed since then.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:34.090
Let's get back to work.

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:34.730
Yes, Sir!
Let's get back to work.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:35.560
Yes, Sir!

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:42.070
It seems that they've contacted
the organization of Dr. Shan.

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:46.530
I see. An old man who's active
behind the world economy.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.410
They truly know just what to shoot for.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:53.250
They're quiet now, because
Genom had pushed them away,

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:56.150
but we can't make light of their power.

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:59.420
Their history is so much longer than ours,

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:02.020
but that's why we know they're worth using.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:06.230
You used Kuzui to leak the data
by reading ahead that far?

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:12.260
I did it by considering Stingray's
personnel network in the past.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:14.570
You're a man to be feared.

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:18.260
You can even hold a giant of the
underworld in your hand.

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:21.640
How about the other one?

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:23.680
Nigel Kirkland?

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:26.210
I had someone contact him.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:30.420
Why would someone as important
as you care about such a nobody?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:35.220
I told you. I'm going to use the
inheritance left by Stingray.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:36.690
Yes, Sir.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:45.360
Are you asking us to check those
sites by going underground?

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:49.200
I will pay twice as much as usual,
so it's not a bad deal, is it?

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:53.700
I'll go. The laboratory, Wiz Lab, right?

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:56.140
Anyway, there's something dangerous there

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:00.250
and it's going to be a big problem
if we don't dispose of it now.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:02.580
Good. I'm going to do it!

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:05.890
Wait! I only want you to work on
this until you find the lab.

00:16:05.890 --> 00:16:07.380
After that, I'll take care of it.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.290
Can I ask one thing?

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:11.220
What?

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:11.790
You told us the lab went missing
during the quake, right?
What?

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:16.260
You told us the lab went missing
during the quake, right?

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:17.700
Yes.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.690
It's your father's lab, isn't it?

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.970
Yes, it is.

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:26.210
Then there might something dangerous.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.400
Please, don't ask any more questions!

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:33.180
Okay, I'll go too.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:35.650
No reason to complain about
the work since I'll be paid.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:37.720
Priss...

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.420
How about you?

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:41.220
Say, why don't you count Mackey in?

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:44.820
Why can't Mackey know about
the mission just this once?

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:47.850
Well...

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:54.930
I'm sorry, Sylia. I've investigated
your personal data, and...

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:55.700
Nene!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:56.440
There's no data, no matter
how hard I looked for it.
Nene!

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:57.700
There's no data, no matter
how hard I looked for it.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:00.240
I thought it was just a mistake
of the family registry system.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:04.540
Dr. Stingray didn't report the birth or adopt him,

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.650
but there's no trace of him!

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:09.380
Dr. Stingray didn't have a son.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.720
So... So...

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.340
Who the hell is that boy?!

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.680
You won't answer my question, will you?

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:23.490
I'm sorry.

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.120
Is he related to the accident
that happened at the lab?

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.270
Nene, you didn't...

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:32.810
Yes. The system protection of the
confidential document was tough,

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:38.110
but I was able to get it by going
through the AD Police mainframe.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:40.050
Wait now. What accident?

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:43.820
The year before the quake, Bioscape,
where Stingray worked,

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:45.750
was bought out by Genom,

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.990
who then took over the boomer
development project.

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:51.820
Dr. Stingray had finally succeeded
in creating the Core,

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.260
and the mass production
of boomers had begun.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:57.000
Suddenly, a mysterious accident
happened at the lab,

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.630
and police troops were called out secretly,

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:01.830
but they failed to secure the situation.

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:04.070
All the lab personnel were dead,

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:07.940
and there were several victims
among the police force.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.910
What happened?

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:11.110
I don't know.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:15.340
The file was a record of AD Police
mobilizations, so I can't tell.

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:19.080
However, I can understand how
horrible that accident was

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:21.420
by looking at how Genom dealt with it after that.

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:24.720
The situation was judged impossible to save

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:27.890
by the chairman of Genom, Quincy Rosenkroitz,

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:31.100
and he ordered the launch of an
artifical earthquake system,

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:32.630
which was in trial at the lab.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.870
Then...

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:37.140
Then the earthquake was caused by that?!

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:40.740
Yes. Everything was caused artificially.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:44.970
No way! How many people do you
think died in that earthquake?!

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:47.300
How many?!

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.690
Now, Sylia, please tell me!

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:59.950
They went so far to hide it.
What was the lab's secret?

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:06.290
I'm sorry, but I can't tell you.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.730
Sylia...

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:12.840
However, Mackey has nothing
to do with the accident.

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.710
That's the only thing I can confirm.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:18.140
That's it. I can't trust you anymore, Sylia!

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:20.140
Nene!

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.390
You may leave if you wish.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:28.150
Sylia!

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:29.760
What Nene said was true.

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.790
I didn't tell you anything about
the most important thing

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:34.830
and asked you to take action
for my convenience.

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:36.330
I took a lot for granted.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:38.020
What are you talking about, Sylia?

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:43.400
It means that what you're seeking
is very dangerous, isn't it?

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.730
We can't leave something like that alone.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:47.610
That's right.

00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:51.540
Knowing there's something
frightening left underground,

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.440
we won't be able to sleep
peacefully at night.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.180
Thank you very much, both of you.

00:19:58.720 --> 00:20:00.180
However, Nene wouldn't...

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.400
Hey, Priss, what do you think?

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:15.730
You mean about Nene? It's a
problem if she works with us

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:18.370
since she's pretty preoccupied,
so this is actually good.

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:20.410
We'll search three points per night per person,

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:22.070
so we can finish in five days by ourselves.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.240
You're the same as always.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.910
What do you mean?

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:30.470
You sound like that all the time
when you're talking about Nene.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:33.920
I'm first.

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:36.340
Wait for me!

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:48.400
They have just begun taking action.

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:50.600
I see. Understood.

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:57.670
Next Episode

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:01.010
Finally, I've found it.

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:03.980
A dark, lost and very deep spot
inside an abandoned place.

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:07.280
A little girl who's been sleeping
there very quietly.

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:10.350
The abominable past, who looks like me.

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:13.020
It's the original source, the
original source of boomers.

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:15.220
Because of the existence of this thing,

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:16.290
I have to destroy it!

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.760
I have to destroy it completely!

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:20.820
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
